# Cumulative mechanical motor-shaft position (not wheel position).
# Optional complement to Status and StatusExtended; existing types unchanged.
# Direction follows RPMCommand: positive increases mean forward motion.
# Each publisher identifies its motor with esc_index (zero-based, like Status).
# Receivers MUST separate state by (source_node_id, esc_index).
#
# origin_id MUST change whenever the publisher reboots, resets/re-zeros its
# position, changes its ticks-per-revolution or changes its representation.
# It MUST NOT be reused while the receiver could still hold data from the old
# origin. Implementations should use a reset-resistant monotonically advancing
# 32-bit generation, or a fresh high-entropy 32-bit nonce for each new origin.
# A random nonce has a small but nonzero collision probability; a publisher
# unable to ensure origin uniqueness cannot guarantee odometry continuity.
# Node-ID changes/NodeStatus uptime resets also require receiver re-baselining.
#
# sample_seq increments modulo 256 for EVERY published MotorPosition transfer
# in the same (source_node_id, esc_index) stream, including invalid measurements. Receivers MUST re-baseline instead of
# integrating across a detected skipped/reordered sequence, an invalid sample,
# an origin change, a source timeout, or a discontinuity. As sequence numbers
# wrap, receivers must also apply a time-gap and physically plausible delta
# check (speed bound). The accepted time window, together with a known bound
# on publication rate, must rule out 256 missed transfers aliasing as a
# consecutive sample; sequence continuity alone is not sufficient.
# The DroneCAN transfer-ID is transport metadata and MUST NOT be used as a
# substitute for this sample sequence.
#
# valid=false means no trustworthy position: the receiver must drop its
# position baseline. The value in position is then unspecified and ignored.
#
# Integer mode: signed int32 counter, modulo 2^32 wrapping, with positive
# ticks_per_revolution. Float mode: finite signed mechanical revolutions;
# NaN/Infinity is invalid. Consumers must reject implausible increments and
# not infer wheel radius, wheel slip, or gear ratio from this message.
#
# Tick-mode payload 95 bits (12 bytes); float-mode payload 79 bits (10 bytes).
# Both require a two-frame transfer on classic DroneCAN/CAN (transfer CRC).
# DTID 1037 is a provisional proposal pending DroneCAN maintainer approval.

uint5 esc_index
bool valid
uint32 origin_id
uint8 sample_seq
MotorPositionValue position
